Important precision on the transfer relation semantics. What does "transfer holds from notion A to notion B" mean? Two possible readings:
(a) Set-theoretic: every A-generic set contains a B-generic set (or is B-generic).
(b) Statement-level: if a property P holds for all data in some A-generic set, then it holds for all data in some B-generic set (i.e., "P is A-generic ⇒ P is B-generic").

Statement-level is the useful one for schemas. Formally: A→B holds iff for every property P: (∃G A-generic with P⊇G) ⇒ (∃G' B-generic with P⊇G'). This is equivalent to: every A-generic set contains a B-generic set. For most notions, generic sets are closed under supersets (filters): comeager sets are upward closed; full-measure sets are upward closed; open dense sets are NOT upward closed (superset of an open dense set need not be open); finite-codim complements are not upward closed either. Hmm. So the statement-level reading via "every A-generic set contains a B-generic set" is cleanest if we define A→B as: ∀G_A ∃G_B: G_B ⊆ G_A. Under this:
- open_dense → residual: any open dense set is comeager (G_A itself is comeager), so holds.
- open_dense → measure: fails if the open dense set has measure < 1 (can't find a full-measure subset of a set of measure <1).
- residual → open_dense: fails (irrationals contain no nonempty open set).
- finite_codim → residual: complement of a closed finite-codim submanifold is open and dense? Wait: if Z is closed with empty interior, D\Z is open dense, hence open_dense, hence residual. So finite_codim→residual holds, and actually finite_codim→open_dense holds too (if Z is closed), under the definition "complement of a closed finite-codim submanifold". Good — I'll define finite_codimension_complement that way (closed embedded finite-codimension submanifold or finite union thereof). Then:
  - finite_codim→open_dense: HOLDS (definitionally, Z closed ⇒ complement open; codim ≥1 ⇒ empty interior ⇒ dense). Extra hypothesis: Z has empty interior (codim ≥ 1) and is closed.
  - finite_codim→residual: HOLDS (since open dense ⇒ comeager).
  - finite_codim→measure: OPEN — requires μ(Z)=0.
- residual→finite_codim: FAILS (irrationals in R: comeager; complement = Q countable, not a finite-codim closed submanifold... hmm, Q is a countable union of points, each codim 1, but countably infinite union — not finite. So Q is not a finite-codim submanifold. But is Q a finite union of submanifolds? No, countably infinite. So fails.) Witness: irrationals in R.
- measure→residual: FAILS (constructed full-measure meager set).
- residual→measure: FAILS (constructed comeager null set).
- measure→open_dense: FAILS (irrationals: full measure, empty interior → contains no nonempty open set).
